    {
      "review_id": "96993",
      "reviewer_name": "Bert",
      "reviewer_location": "VIC - 3134",
      "reviewer_state": "VIC",
      "reviewer_postcode": "3134",
      "reviewer_postcode_valid": true,
      "review_date": "2022-01-15",
      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Whilst it was a little slow getting to the finish line due mainly to Covid, well worth the wait.  Like the installer's namesake, we now have a Ferrari on the roof with the finely tuned motor purring in the garage.  Gerard & team were 1 of only 2 of the 4 we sought quotes from to make a site visit.  These 2 were the only 2 we then considered as they solutioned the system whereas the other 2 just planned it and changes were anticipated at install.We have a reserve next to us with one large imposing tree casting shade on various parts of the roof during the day and pleased to say, both installers discussed that thoroughly with us at site visit and added optimisers to a number of panels as a result.We finally opted with Schumacher as they used conventional Jinko Tiger panels mounted vertically using corrugated roof anchor points and coupled that to a Fronius Primo inverter with a smart meter.The other installer offered larger Jinko Tiger panels and was intent on mounting them horizontally due to our smaller roof batten spacing and they were coupling those up to a Goodwe inverter.  When we asked for a better inverter, we were offered the new Sunways inverter being marketed by Sungrow.  No amount of discussion could sway them from that combo and panel mount so we decided on the Schumacher install as quite frankly, Gerard sold the solution.Topping it all off was the install as not only did they install as per Gerard's design, they also battled through our attic and spent an hour longer than anticipated in a very hot ceiling space and never complaining as they did so.  Thankfully, everything else went smoothly and when they turned it on for the trial run, instantly produced maximum output from the inverter.Still to be inspected and made operational but we have no doubt, our decision was vindicated with the quality system, quality installed and effectively 2 men down as Gerard's team had been rocked by Covid.  Gerard got back on the tools and he and Phil did a fantastic job in trying circumstances.  Thanks Gerard & Phil.  Looking forward to many happy solar power years ahead thanks to your dedication in a very competitive market.",
